 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Meals out and takeaway food in Melbourne rose **3.5% over the year to August 2026**, according to the ABS CPI.\n\n- **Recent trend:** Annual growth was 3.3–3.8% through late 2025 and early 2026, peaked at 4.4% in May 2026, and eased to 3.5% in August 2026.\n- **Price level:** The Melbourne index rose from 95.4 in April 2024 to 103.29 in August 2026, about 8% higher over roughly two and a half years.\n- **Compared with the national figure:** Australia-wide, the same category rose 4.1% in the year to August 2026, so Melbourne is slightly below the national rate.\n- **Earlier in 2024:** Growth was much faster. Melbourne was up 5.8% in the March quarter of 2024, then slowed to 2.3% in the June quarter of 2025 before picking up again.\n\nThe ABS category combines restaurants, cafés and takeaway food, so it doesn't isolate sit-down dining.",
